<b><i>Cyber Riot Squad</i></b>

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.390
Looks like it.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.910
He doesn't look so tough to me.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:45.530
We'll defeat that monster 
executive right now!

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:46.770
Now...

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.030
Let the screening begin!

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.990
<b>— Episode 8 —

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:25.990
<i>Several hours earlier...</i>

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.340
Hey there, you two!

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.250
<b>President's Office</b>

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.250
I hope your classes went well!

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.880
Are you making bank?!

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.630
Mr. President, I'm not sure that's an 
appropriate way to talk to heroes...

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:37.550
What?!

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.410
Are you not getting your merch royalties?

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.110
If the payments are late, 
I'll let accounting know!

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:43.590
That's not what I meant...

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.140
It's just, leading off with talk of money...

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.630
Ah, youth!

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:49.050
You're so young, Yuto, my boy!

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:53.030
Don't I always tell you, when it comes 
prioritizing money or justice...

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:55.410
You always have to choose both!

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:58.650
Because money and justice 
are both <i>equally precious</i>!

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.150
Let's have no bones about it!

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:03.750
<i>This guy doesn't have an 
inside voice, does he?</i>

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.750
By the way, Yuto,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:07.080
you're able to transform using 
the female setting, aren't you?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.040
That's really something!

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.300
Boys can't usually use those!

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.250
I know you were nervous, 
but it's turning out great!

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.810
Your sales are some of 
the best in our history!

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.550
<i>It wasn't the sales I was worried about.</i>

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:23.060
Your ideas about business are 
so amazing, Mr. President.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.930
Have you considered holding 
an online workshop series?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.830
I already have one!

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.470
Mitsuru Sansyu Presents: Money and Justice!

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:28.180
<b>Mitsuru Sansyu Presents</b>

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:28.180
<b><i>Money & Justice</i></b>

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:32.690
<b>Mitsuru Sansyu Presents</b>

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:32.690
<b><i>Money & Justice</i></b>

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:32.690
<b>1980 yen per month</b>

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:32.690
<b>Enroll</b>

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.690
Just 1,980 yen a month!

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.610
Well, I should have known!

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.150
But I'm sure you didn't call us here 
just to share your valuable knowledge.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.950
Oh, yes! That's right!

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:42.570
You're familiar with Agastia, yes?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.260
Yes.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.070
They're an evil organization. 
We encountered them before.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:50.330
They do appear to have some 
very powerful monsters!

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.780
But we need more info on them!

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:56.600
They seem to be the kind of organization 
that flies under the radar when they can.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.290
Thus, I want you to run 
a reconnaissance mission!

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:05.090
<b>Operation: Magical Girls Undercover</b>

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:05.090
I call it Operation: 
Magical Girls Undercover!

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:13.850
Is infiltrating an evil organization 
really appropriate for magical girls?

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.980
The job includes taking out any 
monster executives we meet,

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.160
so no one else could handle it.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.710
That makes it sound like a hit job,

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.110
which I think goes against 
our image even more.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.730
Well, it's too late to complain.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.750
We'll be fine. We have justice on our side.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.330
To all of you who have come here 
to support our ambitions...

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.320
That chief of staff looks 
pretty darn fishy to me.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.830
Let's take him out hard and fast.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.890
I hope he doesn't suspect us.

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.630
We're not exactly inconspicuous, are we?

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:47.400
I can't believe we transformed just to take 
off our costumes and get in disguise.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.590
Magia Break!

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.930
Okay, Yuto...

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:03.960
Strip!

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.700
It's too late to claim you're embarrassed!

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.670
Who thinks about magical girls 
taking off their costumes?

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.950
Just do it! Just do it!

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:14.370
The whole idea scared me!

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.300
Hey! No, Reo! No!

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.830
Oh, shut up.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.560
I let you wear my clothes, 
so be grateful already.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.460
And I tried it on my own once before.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:27.210
I figured if we could change clothes, 
you and I could hang out as girls.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:28.800
Reo...

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.660
Now, let us begin.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:34.230
Enter the room in the order I call you.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.190
Screening numbers one and two!

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.510
That's us.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:39.230
Right!

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:44.520
<i>What kind of horrors does an evil 
organization's screening process entail?</i>

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.480
Kindly introduce yourselves and explain 
why you wish to join our company.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.000
<i>It's an ordinary interview!</i>

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.760
My name is Rin Sato.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.730
My father ran out on us for various reasons.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:03.170
The resulting anxiety combined with 
overwork sent my mother to the hospital,

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.270
and I'm looking for a job 
to pay her medical bills.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:10.340
<i>How can she come up with such a 
serious backstory on the spot?</i>

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:11.100
I saw your ad for combatants and applied.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.390
<i>I've got to think of something, too.</i>

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:13.610
I see.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:16.890
I'm sorry if relating that was painful for you.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:20.010
Now, the next one. Please begin.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:20.880
Right...

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:25.140
My name is, um... Yu... Yusuke Tanaka!

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.900
Yusuke?

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.140
<i>Yuto!</i>

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.110
I-It sounds like a man's name, right?

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.160
People tell me that all the time!

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.580
I suppose everyone has 
their own circumstances.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.290
<i>He must think I'm a complicated person now.</i>

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.500
Now, my next question.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:51.990
What abilities and experiences 
would you bring to our company?

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.040
Sato first.

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:56.480
My previous job put me in 
frequent contact with monsters,

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.210
so I know just how to deal with them!

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.570
<i>Yeah... by destroying them, right?</i>

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:02.310
I see.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:05.900
Work experience with monsters, at your age?

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:10.350
Then you know what's generally 
expected of our combatants?

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:14.830
I know that "combatants" 
is primarily a legacy term.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:19.350
Your classified ad mentioned nothing 
about combat ability, which suggests that

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:22.800
the job mainly involves supporting the 
monster and doing odd jobs at the work site.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.750
I might suggest that workshopping 
the obsolete term

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.170
would help you to find more 
suitable personnel in the future.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:32.620
Your feedback is appreciated.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:37.680
Now, what do you feel is our 
company's goal? Tanaka.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.690
World domination through monsters, right?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.920
Let's assume that is true.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.560
What do you think our specific plans are?

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:46.940
Well, Sato?

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:52.690
You don't engage in any overtly evil 
activities other than fighting heroes.

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:56.530
I suspect this is because you're still 
at the stage of running field tests

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.960
to improve your monsters' performance.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:04.460
In other words, your current priority is the 
development and expansion of your monsters.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:07.530
But certain elements of that 
seem to be proceeding sluggishly

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.970
in light of a world domination goal.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:14.140
Hire me, and I'll be able to offer 
you a more effective plan.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.260
<i>Reo?</i>

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.730
<i>This </i>is<i> a performance, right?</i>

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:21.350
<i>You're not really going to turn against 
the forces of justice, right?</i>

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:24.360
I see. A keen observation.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:27.920
It's a shame I can't hire either of you.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:30.020
Is it because of our age?

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:34.110
I personally believe that age is 
no barrier to a hatred of justice.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:38.480
All the more reason I cannot hire 
anyone below the age of majority.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:43.630
You see, an evil organization fights heroes, 
and some of those may be children.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:47.030
Needless to say, this would be unethical.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:51.170
It follows, too, that any organization that 
would use children for an infiltration mission

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:53.250
is also unethical.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:54.710
He knows who we are!

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:55.640
Let's do it, Zwart!

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.390
Strike Rose!

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.650
Now, my next question.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.920
Our business is an unforgiving 
one these days.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.350
What do you anticipate for your future?

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:15.280
We'll smash through all 
the walls ahead of us!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.020
Sword Zwart!

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:26.790
My final question...

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.300
Any last words before we part ways?

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.560
You're not as tough as you think!

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:33.560
Magia Full Burst!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.560
m 242 101 l 364 88 405 265 279 290

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.560
<b>Good luck

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.560
<b>Absolute Zero Chief of Staff

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.890
I guess he got away.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.230
Stupid, stupid, stupid!

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.470
Drop the super-cool act, you sneaky old man!

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:54.440
Absolute Zero Chief of Staff, my butt!

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:03.390
We'll totally crush him next time, right?

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:04.960
Right, Zwart?!

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:10.160
<i>I'm not entirely sure who the villain is here.</i>

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:17.040
They were an impressively powerful adversary.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.780
It seems we have little time to lose.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:23.090
Now, then...

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.920
Next, please!

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:30.980
<i>The interviews continued.</i>

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:34.100
Boy, what a failure!

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:37.970
We really should've prepared special 
outfits for the infiltration!

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.090
Then we could at least sell merch 
of the one-time-only outfits!

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:45.960
<i>"Everyone has their own sense of justice,</i>

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.840
<i>but in the end, true justice 
belongs to those with money."</i>

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:52.390
<i>A quote from Mitsuru Sansyu's 
online workshop series.</i>

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.550
