00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.550
TECHNIQUE

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.300
Buster Blade!

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.060
Is that the best you've got, Agastia?

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.050
This might be the weakest 
monster you've sent!

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.060
Are you sure about that?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:21.570
This little one is based 
on a brand new concept,

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:24.070
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Monster Development Department
Assistant: Touka Kuroitsu</b>

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:24.070
<b>Secret Society Agastia Monster Development Department
New Assistant: Wolf Bete</b>

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:25.290
designed specifically to take 
down Divine Swordsman Blader!

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.060
The product of our biggest budget in history!

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:31.590
Unprecedented collaboration 
with the relevant departments!

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:34.590
And its ability... is the 
one I proposed before!

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:36.920
"Nesuo" is merely its larval stage!

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.650
Once Divine Swordsman Blader 
inflicts sufficient damage upon it,

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:44.250
a new monster shall burst out from within,

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:46.960
resistant to all attacks previously expended!

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:52.350
Yes... The realization of the dream 
concept I improvised out of desperation!

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.640
Its name is...

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.850
Bandersnatch!

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.650
<b>Reviving Berserker Monster
Bandersnatch</b>

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.080
It regenerated?!

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:02.760
Buster Blade!

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.650
It dodged my blade?!

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:11.270
Yeah! Get 'im!

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:12.420
<i>We did it, Doctor!</i>

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.920
<i>It's a success!</i>

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:21.420
A monster that can learn Blader's attack 
patterns and adjust to them on the spot?

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:24.890
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Monster Development Department
{}Doctor: Hajime Sadamaki</b>

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:24.920
It's certainly an interesting 
concept, Miss Kuroitsu.

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:27.040
But...

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.860
We basically just get one shot at this, right?

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:34.980
If we discover a flaw on the battlefield,
we won't have time to write a bug fix program.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.810
You have a point...

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:40.870
But since we've hit a wall in dealing 
with Blader's attacks already,

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:44.190
I think this kind of out-of-the-box 
thinking is called for!

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:48.960
I'll do repeated operational tests and simulate
 all possible circumstances before the fact!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:52.940
Good grief...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.790
I'll do the best I can, then.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:12:59.980
It's important to always 
keep trying new things.

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.200
Thank you, Doctor!

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:04.580
In that case...

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:07.380
Blader Crush!

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:12.770
We did it, Miss Kuroitsu!

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.870
He's got that jerk Blader on the ropes!

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.120
<i>I'm so glad...</i>

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:18.730
<i>So, so glad!</i>

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.950
<i>If that hell I went through 
had all been for nothing,</i>

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.120
<i>I don't know if I'd ever recover...</i>

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:28.600
He's faster than the Blader Crush.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.370
If I don't do something...

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:35.500
Awright! It's over now, Blader!

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:47.750
Master Blade!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.940
Suigetsu Sen!

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:57.010
Second Form... Master Blader!

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:06.040
I never expected him to bust out a new form.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.820
This scraps all our future 
development plans, too.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:14.070
I really should have anticipated this.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:17.470
There's always a chance that 
a hero has a second form.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.340
Why'd you assume Blader 
didn't have another form?

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:26.230
Because... the thought that we've been 
struggling this much against his base form...

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:28.010
I didn't want to believe it.

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.930
He is the "Divine Swordsman,"

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:33.850
and I'd had this sinking feeling that he 
might have another sword up his sleeve.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:39.820
That total change in his abilities put all of
Banny boy's learned resistances to waste.

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:44.230
Oh, sorry! It's not your fault, Banny boy.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:48.480
As the one who designed your 
concept, it's really my fault.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.520
Snap out of it, Miss Kuroitsu!

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:52.730
This ain't like you!

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:54.870
Just because things turned 
out bad in the end...

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.870
Precisely!

00:14:56.870 --> 00:15:00.630
A battle with a hero is 
waged one step at a time.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.250
Lord Megistus!

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.850
I beg your forgiveness.

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:05.750
It was my lack of foresight 
that caused this.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:10.630
Dr. Sadamaki and Bandersnatch did 
exactly what I asked of them.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:15.130
I... I should have anticipated a form change.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:17.780
I appreciate your contrition,

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:20.260
but there's no need for you to feel guilty.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:24.190
When working as part of an organization, 
excessive concern about who's to blame

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:26.750
can lead to pointing fingers 
during crucial moments,

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:31.520
resulting in an inability to employ 
anything but reliable, proven ideas.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:36.930
When a person's abilities are exceptional, 
they must use those abilities effectively.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.780
Diluting that for the sake 
of a positive reputation

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:44.130
will hinder your ability to give 
your all to your real job.

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:47.780
That would be a loss to our organization.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:52.540
You created an innovative new monster.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.290
That in itself is worth praise.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.290
Th-Thank you...

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.060
Obviously, we do wish to defeat Blader,

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:05.030
but that is not our only priority at present.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:08.240
Do not forget this—

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:13.650
It is not <i>we</i> who are fighting a battle 
that we cannot afford to lose.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.550
Miss Kuroitsu...

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:28.340
Thanks, Wolfie boy!

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:29.620
You were so right!

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:31.710
It wasn't like me to sulk like that!

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.220
Let's keep giving this our best!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.470
J-J-Just glad you're feeling better...

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:42.100
What we need now is to come up 
with a diversity of approaches

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:44.930
in anticipation of possible 
future form changes.

00:16:44.930 --> 00:16:46.230
Yes,

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.630
depending on what ways specifically 
Blader grows stronger.

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:52.950
And in the worst case scenario, 
we might have to deal with <i>that</i>.

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:55.700
Yes. <i>That</i>...

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:56.690
"That"?

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:58.410
That! A robot!

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:00.560
A robot? For real?!

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:02.200
We're gonna see a giant friggin' robot?

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:03.820
That's freakin' awesome!

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:06.460
Let's make a giant monster to fight it!

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:09.050
Wolfie boy...

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:12.550
A fifty-meter-tall giant-sized monster

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:15.000
would be 25 times taller 
than our standard ones, right?

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:19.390
Its volume would therefore be 25 cubed,

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:22.970
meaning we'd need 15,000 times the 
standard material amount to make it.

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:25.710
When taking construction 
costs into account,

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.210
plus the maintenance costs 
when it's complete...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.960
Not happening.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:41.620
Where do heroes find the money to 
fund their operations, anyway?

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.050
It's a good question.

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:46.510
They must have some serious backers.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:51.000
Heroes are truly terrifying!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.510
<b>Sadamaki</b>

00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:04.860
<i>What in the world happened back there?</i>

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:13.770
<i>Next Stage: Master Blader!</i>

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.960
Suigetsu Sen!

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:40.100
<i>A second form...</i>

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.220
I'm home.

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:43.550
Uh-oh!

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:46.400
Welcome home, Big Bro!

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.520
What's wrong, Kenji?

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:50.010
Oh, nothing!

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:54.260
Say, Bro... you work at a big 
research facility, right?

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:55.980
Yeah. Why?

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:58.390
I could use some advice.

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:01.250
If you suddenly got some new 
gear delivered out of nowhere,

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:04.600
and nobody contacted you 
about what it was...

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.630
I don't know quite what 
you're talking about.

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.490
Is someone trying to scam you?

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.990
You think so?

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.500
Can I see your contract?

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:15.260
I don't have documentation. Or emails.

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:17.750
That sounds really shady.

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.720
What in the world did they send you?

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.930
Well... I can't really...

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:25.340
<i>The worries never end, 
for the forces of good and evil both.</i>

